<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    cloud.txt holds the S3 secret key and stays on the device: it is never
    backed up or moved to a new device. The game writes it through a temp
    file named cloud.txt.tmp.<pid>.<n> (writeFileAtomic, created 0600 with
    O_EXCL), and these rules take exact paths only, no wildcards, so no rule
    can list those names. That is accepted: a temp file holds the secret from
    its creation until the rename over cloud.txt, a window that spans the
    write and the fsync, which on phone flash can take tens to hundreds of
    milliseconds. It is left behind only when the process is killed inside
    that window or a failed write cannot unlink it; task cf3 removes such
    leftovers (cloud.txt.tmp.*) at startup and when the cloud config is
    removed. cloud.txt.tmp, the fixed temp name of older builds, stays
    excluded for the leftovers those builds may have left (task cf3 removes
    it too).

    Considered and not taken: keeping cloud.txt and its temp files in a
    folder of their own, such as saves/private/, which one rule here could
    exclude as a whole (a folder path covers everything below it, temp names
    included). That would need a migration of the cloud.txt of existing
    installs into the new folder. Keep the same paths in data_extraction_rules.xml.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="file" path="saves/cloud.txt" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="saves/cloud.txt.tmp" />
</full-backup-content>
